# Proof engine artifacts (regenerable, machine-specific paths)
.ripcord/

# Webapp build output (dist-server from tsconfig.server.json, dist-web from
# vite.config.ts) and the local RIPCORD_DATA_DIR used by manual server runs.
# Both are regenerable from source and machine/run-specific — same reasoning
# as dist/ and .cache/ above.
dist-server/
dist-web/
.ripcord-data/

# Mobula live sidecars (calibration/live/*.json) are COMMITTED too, for the same
# reason as the pages: a clean clone can then re-render every page without a
# Mobula API key. They are timestamped snapshots and are DELIBERATELY not
# deterministic — `pnpm determinism` covers calibration/reports/ only, and
# `pnpm verify:boundary` checks that no API key ever lands in one. See
# docs/MOBULA.md.

# Rendered calibration pages and the pinned reports they come from are COMMITTED
# on purpose: they are the day-5 evidence, and they let anyone re-render or
# re-check the numbers without an RPC key. Nothing here is regenerated at view
# time.
